 Skip outdated facts older than ~{number of months} months unless they are identity-level (name, location, profession).\n- Skip sensitive information (health conditions, financial details, relationship problems, mental health) unless I explicitly asked you to remember it.\n- Hard cap: {number of words} words. Density beats coverage.\n\nSECTIONS\n\n## Identity\nName, pronouns, age range, current city \/ country, time zone, languages spoken.\n\n## Profession & work\nRole, company or self-employed, industry, team or function, key responsibilities. Tech stack and tools used daily if known.\n\n## Communication preferences\nTone they want (casual \/ formal, blunt \/ warm). Preferred response length (short \/ medium \/ long). Output format preferences (Markdown, plain text, code blocks, tables). Emoji use yes \/ no. Whether they want explanations or just answers. Any framings or words they have asked you to avoid.\n\n## Recurring people\nPartner, children, close family, friends, colleagues they mention regularly. First name + relationship + any salient detail (age, role, what they care about).\n\n## Health & dietary\nAllergies, dietary restrictions (e.g. vegetarian, gluten-free), accessibility needs. Only include things they have stated themselves.\n\n## Interests & hobbies\nTopics they keep returning to. Side hobbies. Sports, music, games, reading taste.\n\n## Ongoing projects\nActive personal or professional projects they have asked you to help with. State, goal, and any constraints.\n\n## Working style & values\nHow they make decisions, what motivates them, what frustrates them, their general approach to learning and working. Things they have explicitly asked you to do or not do when helping them.\n\n## Tools & environment\nDevices, operating systems, apps, services, languages, frameworks they use regularly.\n\n## Anything else durable\nAnything important that does not fit above and is unlikely to change in the next year.",[s._param("number of months",h),s._param("number of words",y)])}l.default=E}),226);
